---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { company } from '../../config/site';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated="9 September 2026">
  <p>
    This notice describes how personal data is processed for users who visit the
    <strong>openeam.it</strong> website, pursuant to Articles 13 and 14 of Regulation
    (EU) 2016/679 ("GDPR").
  </p>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The Data Controller is <strong>{company.legal}</strong>, based at Via Barletta 9,
    95125 Catania (CT), Italy — VAT no. 05728230870. For any request regarding the
    processing of your personal data, or to exercise the rights set out in Articles
    15-22 of the GDPR (access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and
    objection), you can write to <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Data collected through the demo request form</h2>
  <p>
    Through the demo request form we collect your first name, last name, company, role,
    and business email address. This data is processed solely to contact you back and
    arrange a demonstration of the openeam.it platform, and is not used for marketing
    purposes or shared with third parties other than the external processors listed in
    this notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Purpose and legal basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Handling demo and contact requests (pre-contractual measures taken at the data subject's request, Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
    <li>Compliance with legal and contractual obligations (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    Data submitted through the demo request form is retained for the time strictly
    necessary to manage the pre-contractual request, and in any case no longer than 12
    months from the last contact with the data subject, after which it is deleted or
    anonymised, unless a longer retention period is required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>External data processors</h2>
  <p>
    Emails generated by the demo request form are sent via the third-party platform
    <strong>EmailJS</strong>, which acts as an external data processor pursuant to Art.
    28 of the GDPR, appointed under a dedicated agreement. Data shared with EmailJS is
    limited to what is necessary to send the communication.
  </p>

  <h2>Data subject rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can exercise, at any time, the rights set out in Articles 15-22 of the GDPR
    (access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection) by writing
    to the Data Controller at <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>.
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection
    Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
